Stop giving this guy heck over this. It's perfectly valid for him to
make up his own term for an "almost ascension failed due to an accident
that wasn't my fault." Now if he was actually referring to then as
*ascensions*, that would be another story.

I myself am tempted to start the "completion" instead of ascension
thing. Not because I *can't* ascend (I've done it twice so far) but
because Gehennom and the ascension run are so darn boring and tedious.
The real fun is getting a character to the point where they *can*
ascend. I have an ascendable wizard and an almost-ascendable tourist
sitting somewhere in Gehennom, abandoned because I just got sick of
them.

It actually makes quite a bit of sense to refer to an ascendable
character as a "completion." If you say, "I've completed barbarian,
priest, valkyrie, wizard, and samurai," this essentially means, "I have
mastered the strategy of the B/P/V/W/S classes." Most ascendable
characters are playable by essentially the same strategy anyway -- hack
and slash if you're a weapon-user, blast with spells if a magic-user.
It becomes, essentially, a matter of, "If you've seen one, you've seen
'em all."

